{"game": "earth-defense-force-5", "language": "english", "appid": 1007040, "month": "2023-10", "window": 4, "start_date": 1698105600, "end_date": 1698796799, "month_true_total": 59, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-09-28 17:54:10 UTC", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "149267567", "author": {"steamid": "76561197985157996", "personaname": "An Irate Capybara", "persona_status": "online", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/AnIrateCapybara/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 110, "playtime_forever": 23554, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 23422, "last_played": 1702483998, "avatar": "77fb20d6e3fab3987f388925917ed131b3c6e096"}, "language": "english", "review": "EDF5 is a great follow-up to EDF4.1, with plenty of new enemy types and much fun combat to be had.  However, I think players should go in with a fair warning about one of the new enemies.  Now, I don't know if this was intentional, but for the first time in the series there is an enemy that will leave many players with the distinct feeling that they are fighting and killing other human beings.  This can be very unsettling.  Of course devs and fanboys will respond that this enemy type \"just isn't\" human and that \"if you don't fight them, YOU will be killed\", but all one needs to do is go down a list of the limbs and facial features we have in common to know that these enemies look almost exactly like human beings.", "timestamp_created": 1698777594, "timestamp_updated": 1698777594, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 1, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1562828575", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "149211058", "author": {"steamid": "76561198363068921", "personaname": "Zartress (C0ck)", "persona_status": "in-game", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198363